[2026-01-30T14:40:50.728Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Implementation: Extract force-directed layout into reusable graph layout engine\n\n## Context Area\nData Visualizations\n\n## Description\nExtract force-directed layout into reusable graph layout engine\n\n## Implementation Details\n\n## Vision\nExtract the force-directed graph layout logic from NetworkGraph.tsx, SourceNetwork.tsx, and RadarView.tsx into a reusable graph layout engine that supports multiple layout algorithms and can be shared across all network-style visualizations.\n\n## Business Value\n- Three separate implementations of force-directed layout exist with varying quality\n- A unified engine enables new visualization types without reimplementing physics\n- Better performance through optimized, shared layout calculations\n- Consistent interaction patterns across all network visualizations\n\n## Scope\n**Included:**\n- Force-directed layout algorithm (attraction/repulsion)\n- Circular/radial layout for categorical grouping\n- Constellation-style layout for hierarchical data\n- Layout hooks with configurable parameters\n\n**Out of scope:**\n- 3D layouts\n- Real-time collaborative layout\n\n## Key Components\n1. src/lib/layout/force-directed.ts - Core force simulation\n2. src/lib/layout/circular.ts - Circular arrangement algorithm\n3. src/lib/layout/hooks.ts - useForceLayout, useCircularLayout hooks\n4. src/lib/layout/types.ts - Shared node/edge type definitions\n\n## Technical Approach\n1. Analyze existing implementations in NetworkGraph, SourceNetwork, RadarView\n2. Extract common node/edge interfaces\n3. Implement configurable force simulation with iteration control\n4. Create React hooks that manage layout state and updates\n5. Refactor existing visualizations to use the shared layout engine\n6. Add layout algorithm selection to network-style components\n\n## Files to Modify\n- src/components/report/visualizations/NetworkGraph.tsx - Use shared layout\n- src/components/report/visualizations/SourceNetwork.tsx - Use shared layout\n- src/components/visualizations/RadarView.tsx - Use shared layout for node positioning\n- Create new src/lib/layout/ directory with layout algorithms\n\n## Success Criteria\n- [ ] Single source of truth for force-directed layout logic\n- [ ] All three network visualizations use shared layout engine\n- [ ] Layout parameters are configurable per-component\n- [ ] Performance is equal or better than current implementations\n\n## Potential Challenges\n- Different visualizations have slightly different requirements - make engine flexible\n- Animation during layout updates needs careful handling to avoid jank\n\n## Instructions\n\n1. Read and understand the implementation details above\n2. Identify all files that need to be modified\n3. Implement the changes following the guidance provided\n4. Ensure code quality and type safety\n5. Test the changes work as expected\n\n## Notes\n\nThis requirement was generated from an accepted Development Direction.\nFocus on implementing exactly what is described above.\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"063d9692-0974-4418-8890-3933b0ef315a","uuid":"b7c003f0-bcc0-4270-bff1-eed881e8fe4d","isSynthetic":true}
